abstract: >-
  We classify the extremal families of lattice paths with pairwise even
  numbers of common edges for every length and endpoint, which gives
  Shankar's Catalan conjecture, compute the binary rank of grid graphs, and
  double the lower bound for odd families in the square. We prove that the
  signed Eulerian polynomials are real-rooted, as Fulman, Kim, Lee and
  Petersen conjectured, and settle conjectures on canon, caged and Dumont
  permutations.
